@sonicblis
Here's a temporary fix that works for me:

```
(function () {
    var g;
    if (typeof (window) != null) g = window;
    else if (typeof (global) != null) g = global;
        // couldn't locate global
    else return;

    var obsProto = g.Rx.Observable.prototype;

    obsProto._catch = obsProto.catch;
})();
```

@Huck 

The best advice I can give is to either clone or reference the routing and nav [plunkr](https://angular.io/resources/live-examples/router/ts/plnkr.html) provided in angular documentation and move from there to determine what has gone wrong in your project.

Additionally, check each dependency's `package.json` to verify you are really using the version you've specified.  I've had scenarios where I _thought_ all the packages were updated when in reality they were not due to some unnoticed npm error.
